Native Btrfs driver

vendor/btrfs contains a bare-metal port of the filesystem and transaction
code from https://github.com/antimatter-studios/rust-fs-btrfs at
bac713a69c2b65f70ef1ea0845760f92858ad88d (0.11.0 development tree).
Copyright (c) 2026 Chris Thomas. Its MIT license is in vendor/btrfs/LICENSE.
The port uses the kernel block interface, allocation, clock and a bounded
metadata cache. The filesystem-tree orphan lifecycle is implemented in Rust.
vendor/btrfs/lzo1x contains the codec from rust-lzo1x 0.4.0, adapted for
no_std; its upstream license is retained alongside the source.

Native user-mode context switching and the C system-call entry stubs use the
MIT-licensed xv6 x86 CPU routines. The 32-bit routines are from MIT's
xv6-public at eeb7b415dbcb12cc362d0783e41c3d1f44066b17. The 64-bit
routines are from mars-research/xv6-64 at 1d89f61468ffe0ee975287712a2fb34fac4ba253.
The build preparation script verifies both source and license digests.
